-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc56156379"><span class=3D"=
confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156379"></span></span>Introduction</h1>
<p local-id=3D"17d48a3d7778"><br>
Sonicauto 3.0 is a web application which aims to be the face of automation =
at SonicWALL, Inc. This application offers interfaces to launch tests, moni=
tor them, track results and in generating reports as a bare minimum and wou=
ld offer much more as it evolves. <br>
Sonicauto 3.0 though offers a similar look and feel of Sonicauto 2.0; the a=
pplication is entirely re-built from scratch. The following are some of the=
 salient features of Sonicauto 3.0.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"9a08a610d755">
<li local-id=3D"ad95d8a2377b">
<p local-id=3D"adff214507d4">Uses a PostgreSQL database.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fa9dcd1a4e63">
<p local-id=3D"cae4648328cf">Backend uses Django web framework which is wri=
tten by Python.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9d1a6652932b">
<p local-id=3D"b56f85c18029">Frontend uses VUE.js =E2=80=A6=E2=80=A6 (to be=
 added here)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3e1b113323fd">
<p local-id=3D"a4ae34a0cf21">Re-use SQL commands in Sonicauto2.0 which make=
s it easily to be re-built</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"767d06107088">
<p local-id=3D"290b69d4c1c8">Offers Data push feature. Some key pages like,=
 Reports Dashboard, QBS Job Status and QBS Host Status are implemented usin=
g Data push. Here the data is automatically updated in the client every 10-=
30 seconds without the need for the client to poll the server.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"7905a7651cda"><br><br>
The following is the list of various software components used and their ver=
sion.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"382136cf0a2d">
<li local-id=3D"f40e6dca358d">
<p local-id=3D"4815d0610df1">Django &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - 2.1 (will be=
 updated 2.2 LTS in 2019)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2a09f7c940e7">
<p local-id=3D"362a443abf57">Python&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - 3.6</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"62a80a809fe0">
<p local-id=3D"8c5d4d0814c2">VUE&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 3.x</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"75f84c888a60">
<p local-id=3D"a4a5c650c6dc">NodeJs &nbsp; -&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; =
15.4.0</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4a58b38459f8">
<p local-id=3D"eb4f3b503a6d">Git bash&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"407871bdc006">
<p local-id=3D"1e0bc3da4f10">Webpack - &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 4.0+</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"858a93e930b3">
<p local-id=3D"52e04c331881">ES6&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3a17c173f189">
<p local-id=3D"f6f323d3804b">TypeScript&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"c79fbba0b6a0"><br><br>
This document serves as a guide for understanding the Sonicauto 3.0 framewo=
rk, development environment, how to deploy changes and how to add code to c=
ertain areas of the application.</p>
