<h2 local-id=3D"04bb6a51d685" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-1.1Frontend(W=
ebpack/VUE)Framework">1.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Frontend (Webpack/VUE) Framewor=
k</h2>
<p local-id=3D"63d826ee7b87"><br></p>
<p local-id=3D"f4fa1ba054fe">For Sonicauto3.0, the frontend server uses ngi=
nx, project will be packed in /nginx/html by webserver framework.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4857544184bc"><br></p>
<p local-id=3D"2a983b636b05">As for UI, we extends @sonicwall-uuif, and Ele=
ment-UI as our third UI library.</p>
<p local-id=3D"dedd5bf5ffa9"><br></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"d78bbb948484" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-1.1.1Initials=
etup">1.1.1&nbsp;&nbsp; Initial setup</h3>
<p local-id=3D"c2413acb494f">Set up development environment. Make sure your=
 computer has all needful tools: node.js, npm. Use npm to install Vue/Cli (=
version must above 3.0), webpack.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a648742ecc26">Use command : npm install @vue/cli(=E2=80=98@=
=E2=80=99 must be given, or it will install vue 2.8 automatically), then us=
e =E2=80=98vue -V/--version=E2=80=99 to check.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b69a9a4b08b5"><br></p>
<p local-id=3D"607cfaefb153"><strong><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-red2"=
>ATTENTION: SonicWALL UUIF doesn't support Windows environment at least for=
 now, If you are using windows, please first check with developer about the=
 lib.</span></strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"22fc80e85ca2"><br></p>
<p local-id=3D"b63185ea0c64">Step1: install nodejs and git</p>
<p local-id=3D"1bda65af8be3">go to&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"=
https://nodejs.org/zh-cn/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://nodejs.org/zh-cn/</a>&n=
bsp;and&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://www.git-scm.com/" re=
l=3D"nofollow">http://www.git-scm.com/</a></p>
<p local-id=3D"8c7bd774d79f">download and intsall nodejs and git</p>
<p local-id=3D"53179100e23f">Step 2: download source code to local</p>
<p local-id=3D"3d8b4db11408">git clone <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"m=
ailto:git@sonicgit.eng.sonicwall.com" rel=3D"nofollow">git@sonicgit.eng.son=
icwall.com</a>:automation/Sonicauto3.0.git</p>
<p local-id=3D"9b8ab16135fd">cd&nbsp;Sonicauto3.0</p>
<p local-id=3D"a26cef6cbfde">Step 3: install environment</p>
<p local-id=3D"ef5f827049b8">npm install</p>
<p local-id=3D"a432374dc6dc">this step is to setup a environment and may ne=
ed 30 minutes or more. This step only need to be run one time.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f95c3bce4ecf">Step 4: build files</p>
<p local-id=3D"6b14e58bd5f1">npm run build</p>
<p local-id=3D"dda1c1449873">when finished, user can get built files in&nbs=
p;Sonicauto3.0\dist folder</p>
<p local-id=3D"1265511d787c">Step 5: upload files to nginx server</p>
<p local-id=3D"80ab34008f25">copy files from Sonicauto3.0\dist to&nbsp;/usr=
/local/nginx/html</p>
<p local-id=3D"4811f6beffe5">'/usr/local/nginx/html' is nginx&nbsp;location=
 folder. User can also use Apache server</p>
<p local-id=3D"64ba76598ee6">after that, restart server</p>
<p local-id=3D"3809f9c3b64a">nginx -s reload</p>
<p local-id=3D"32169f8e058c">or</p>
<p local-id=3D"6f572baa9fe9">nginx -s stop</p>
<p local-id=3D"f16b8b5918a6">nginx</p>
<p local-id=3D"4322e24ce204">Step 6: Read examples:</p>
<p local-id=3D"dd2743734540">Developers give us lots of examples about how =
to use&nbsp;UUIF (Unified User Interface Framework). Please read and try th=
em before you start design new sonicauto3 feature.</p>
<p local-id=3D"042bc6993c5e">UUIF API Doc Site<br><a class=3D"external-link=
" href=3D"https://uuif.eng.sonicwall.com" rel=3D"nofollow">https://uuif.eng=
.sonicwall.com</a></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image=
