span><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide=
-_Toc17104836"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc17104836"><=
/span></span>DB Access function</h4>
<p local-id=3D"658a6f970720"><br>
In sonicauto 3.0, we need to perform queries that don't map clearly to Djan=
go's models, or directly execute UPDATE, INSERT, or DELETE queries. In thes=
e cases, developers can always access the database directly, routing around=
 the model layer entirely. <br>
SonicautoDBAccessor.py contains all the classes that need to access databas=
e. It takes several steps for django to fetch data from database:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"16108f02ff68">
<li local-id=3D"cc28c68d66fa">
<p local-id=3D"d50dcb904c08">Configure the default database information in =
sonicauto/settings.py</p></li>
</ol><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper con=
fluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image=
-left" width=3D"373" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"89fb1a41dec9846a3a4f07126f3345=
66cd97e622ddd74194e5760aab8f3e6915" data-image-src=3D"https://sonicwall.atl=
assian.net/wiki/download/attachments/2274492531/worddav8fb08298168a5801aae5=
1dda1f7fed69.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1775532001290&amp;cache=
