content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2274492531"=
 data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"1" data-media-id=3D"a07a6916-6b8=
8-4864-9a45-3b2d54eb9236" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"230"></span>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"6d849b0d63d9">
<li local-id=3D"8688a6a59f3d">
<p local-id=3D"7eea6dd628bd">In sonicautoDBAccessor.py, use django.db.conne=
ction to access default database.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"d1f4e237491a"><br></p>
<p><br class=3D"atl-forced-newline"><span class=3D"image-wrap" style=3D""><=
img src=3D"bb33d0a0fc50c7cf6c87cec308e236732350eb35304026a99388005d66b39f5f=
" height=3D"139" width=3D"468" style=3D"border: 0px solid black"></span> <b=
r class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
 And the data fetched from database will make up a list of tuple like: <br>
 [('198','VTB101'), ( '75','VTB84'), ( '255','VTB313')]. <br class=3D"atl-f=
orced-newline"></p>
<p local-id=3D"0aa023b3c04b"><br></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"ee9e9d10d21f">
<li local-id=3D"ff64addb9944">
<p local-id=3D"853318608b5e">Construct data structure</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"e7c1156bb5fd"><br></p>
<p>In Sonicauto 2.0, we create Plain Old Java Object (POJO) to organize the=
 structure of response data. In Sonicauot 3.0, we create Python classes for=
 this purpose. Let's see an example. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
 First, define a class in api_v1/sonicauto_utils.py <br class=3D"atl-forced=
-newline"><span class=3D"image-wrap" style=3D""><img src=3D"e656a35d1e0d3ee=
922aa272026f888169c57a841c6e2f998932798920dfd2eed" height=3D"116" width=3D"=
374" style=3D"border: 0px solid black"></span> <br class=3D"atl-forced-newl=
ine">
 Second, In sonicautoDBAccessor.py, use it to construct data structure afte=
r fetch them from database. <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline"><span class=3D=
"image-wrap" style=3D""><img src=3D"57e98ff15a55c5ae2e42c104f6c8970bf36835b=
1624a12bba5f09c167e5a751a" height=3D"208" width=3D"468" style=3D"border: 0p=
x solid black"></span> <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline">
 And 'result_list' will like<br>
 [{'tbid': '198', 'name': 'VTB101'}, { 'tbid': '75', 'name': 'VTB84'}, { 't=
bid': '255', 'name': 'VTB313'}] <br class=3D"atl-forced-newline"></p>
<p local-id=3D"34e7e91f1e05"><br></p>
