uence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55551778"></span></span><span class=3D"conflue=
nce-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc56156386"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156386"></span></span>Design RESTfu=
l API</h3>
<p local-id=3D"dd3724459ef6">Representational State Transfer (REST) is a so=
ftware architectural style that defines a set of constraints to be used for=
 creating web services. The REST architectural style describes six constrai=
nts. These constraints, applied to the architecture, were originally commun=
icated by Roy Fielding in his doctoral dissertation (see <a class=3D"extern=
al-link" href=3D"https://www.ics.uci.edu/~fielding/pubs/dissertation/rest_a=
rch_style.htm" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.ics.uci.edu/~fielding/pubs/diss=
ertation/rest_arch_style.htm</a> ) and defines the basis of RESTful-style. =
<br>
The six constraints are:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"083ecb074dee">
<li local-id=3D"ee4cec90ad01">
<p local-id=3D"2e8cdb10b225">Uniform Interface</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"979c7dfad0cb">
<p local-id=3D"b1fcba3ee63f">Stateless</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c871fd3f7fa6">
<p local-id=3D"af2f76137f3e">Cacheable</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"05706eabd0be">
<p local-id=3D"c62cf69e3b77">Client-Server</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"692de606ca47">
<p local-id=3D"c25899047a15">Layered System</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"267d89b25903">
<p local-id=3D"7efa0282be96">Code on Demand (optional)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"0c6df22e7a1d"><br>
To make it easily, let me use 10 examples to illustrate it.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b74a5f872b20">
<li local-id=3D"145e41eec269">
<p local-id=3D"7702ae18bc4d">Protocol</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"bcd0262666a2">It is recommended to use HTTPS insteads of HTT=
P</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"4440dcce3d67">
<li local-id=3D"19760e686841">
<p local-id=3D"dfec762b4251">Domain name</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"94ae62613873"><a href=3D"#" rel=3D"nofollow">https://<span c=
lass=3D"legacy-color-text-red2">api</span>.example.com</a><span class=3D"co=
nfluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=
=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-external-resource" height=3D"7" wi=
dth=3D"7" src=3D"73a2e9183154d4b949d2be7a1672754c93c0a544b3904881103da52794=
9b62a5" data-image-src=3D"https://engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/images/icon=
s/linkext7.gif" loading=3D"lazy"></span><br><a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://example.org/%3Cspan+style%3D%22color%3A+%23ff0000%22%3Eapi%3C%2=
Fspan%3E/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://example.org/<span class=3D"legacy-color=
-text-red2">api</span>/</a><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper =
confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image co=
nfluence-external-resource" height=3D"7" width=3D"7" src=3D"73a2e9183154d4b=
949d2be7a1672754c93c0a544b3904881103da527949b62a5" data-image-src=3D"https:=
//engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/images/icons/linkext7.gif" loading=3D"lazy"=
></span><br>
Because of same-origin policy, the second style is better.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"6c7698784e05">
<li local-id=3D"0ce547b5263f">
<p local-id=3D"9c291844459a">Versioning</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"9761ef06ebf3">put API version into URL <a class=3D"external-=
link" href=3D"https://example.org/api/%3Cspan+style%3D%22color%3A+%23ff0000=
%22%3Ev1%3C%2Fspan%3E/*" rel=3D"nofollow">https://example.org/api/<span cla=
ss=3D"legacy-color-text-red2">v1</span>/*</a><span class=3D"confluence-embe=
dded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence=
-embedded-image confluence-external-resource" height=3D"7" width=3D"7" src=
=3D"73a2e9183154d4b949d2be7a1672754c93c0a544b3904881103da527949b62a5" data-=
image-src=3D"https://engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/images/icons/linkext7.gi=
f" loading=3D"lazy"></span><br>
Another way is putting version number into HTTP HEAD. Go to <a class=3D"ext=
ernal-link" href=3D"https://developer.github.com/v3/media/#request-specific=
-version" rel=3D"nofollow">https://developer.github.com/v3/media/#request-s=
pecific-version</a> for detailed inforamtion.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"238521ea4d20">
<li local-id=3D"699cf9dbecbd">
<p local-id=3D"cdfd73de7077">Endpoint</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"c23c9235f849">An Endpoint is a URL within your API which poi=
nts to a specific Resource or a Collection of Resources.<br>
If you were building a fictional API to represent several different Zoo's, =
each containing many Animals (with an animal belonging to exactly one Zoo),=
 employees (who can work at multiple zoos) and keeping track of the species=
 of each animal, you might have the following endpoints: <a class=3D"extern=
al-link" href=3D"https://example.org/api/v1/%3Cspan+style%3D%22color%3A+%23=
ff0000%22%3Ezoos%3C%2Fspan%3E" rel=3D"nofollow">https://example.org/api/v1/=
<span class=3D"legacy-color-text-red2">zoos</span></a><span class=3D"conflu=
ence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"c=
onfluence-embedded-image confluence-external-resource" height=3D"7" width=
=3D"7" src=3D"73a2e9183154d4b949d2be7a1672754c93c0a544b3904881103da527949b6=
2a5" data-image-src=3D"https://engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/images/icons/l=
inkext7.gif" loading=3D"lazy"></span> <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"ht=
tps://example.org/api/v1/%3Cspan+style%3D%22color%3A+%23ff0000%22%3Eanimals=
%3C%2Fspan%3E" rel=3D"nofollow">https://example.org/api/v1/<span class=3D"l=
egacy-color-text-red2">animals</span></a><span class=3D"confluence-embedded=
-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-emb=
edded-image confluence-external-resource" height=3D"7" width=3D"7" src=3D"7=
3a2e9183154d4b949d2be7a1672754c93c0a544b3904881103da527949b62a5" data-image=
-src=3D"https://engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/images/icons/linkext7.gif" lo=
ading=3D"lazy"></span> <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://example.o=
rg/api/v1/%3Cspan+style%3D%22color%3A+%23ff0000%22%3Eemployees%3C%2Fspan%3E=
" rel=3D"nofollow">https://example.org/api/v1/<span class=3D"legacy-color-t=
ext-red2">employees</span></a><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapp=
er confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image=
 confluence-external-resource" height=3D"7" width=3D"7" src=3D"73a2e9183154=
d4b949d2be7a1672754c93c0a544b3904881103da527949b62a5" data-image-src=3D"htt=
ps://engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/images/icons/linkext7.gif" loading=3D"la=
zy"></span></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c1fb8e78c07c">
<li local-id=3D"609005f3ca5b">
<p local-id=3D"4fb619c271aa">Using HTTP Methods for RESTful Services</p></l=
i>
</ol>
<ul local-id=3D"613b0fd1e0f5">
<li local-id=3D"765ba57393af">
<p local-id=3D"18784981ff62">POST(Create): 201 (Created), 'Location' header=
 with link to /customers/{id} containing new ID.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e08a4633ac41">
<p local-id=3D"cdb3546a7d31">GET(Read): 200 (OK), list of customers. Use pa=
gination, sorting and filtering to navigate big lists.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4d9cbd3a0879">
<p local-id=3D"b4672bbafbdd">PUT(Update/Replace): 405 (Method Not Allowed),=
 unless you want to update/replace every resource in the entire collection.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8fea1d3ae2f8">
<p local-id=3D"d8aebb1eeed6">PATCH(Update/Modify): 405 (Method Not Allowed)=
, unless you want to modify the collection itself.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d3f4d6432188">
<p local-id=3D"e800883885fe">DELETE(Delete): 405 (Method Not Allowed), unle=
ss you want to delete the whole collection=E2=80=94not often desirable.</p>=
</li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"71f207e8d597"><br></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"ac9846b239a9">
<li local-id=3D"554fe9b8d6d8">
<p local-id=3D"df2f9d067a10">Filtering</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"23b7867c113d">When a Consumer makes a request for a listing =
of objects, it is important that you give them a list of every single objec=
t matching the requested criteria. This list could be massive.<br>
Filtering is mostly useful for performing GETs on Collections of resources.=
 Since these are GET requests, filtering information should be passed via t=
he URL. Here are some examples of the types of filtering you could conceiva=
bly add to your API:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a36ecedaab2e">
<li local-id=3D"fafbd871a3fd">
<p local-id=3D"f45226292f76">?limit=3D10: Reduce the number of results retu=
rned to the Consumer (for Pagination)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"985fd3c72576">
<p local-id=3D"eb0b22fe17f5">?offset=3D10: Send sets of information to the =
Consumer (for Pagination)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6925bccf6bdc">
<p local-id=3D"291daf2c1785">?animal_type_id=3D1: Filter records which matc=
h the following condition (WHERE animal_type_id =3D 1)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"54b2d9d7cc66">
<p local-id=3D"d5dd95c014e8">?sortby=3Dname&amp;order=3Dasc: Sort the resul=
ts based on the specified attribute (ORDER BY `name` ASC)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"18ecef8d6fe5"><br>
Some of these filterings can be redundant with endpoint URLS. For example, =
/zoo/ZID/animals is the same thing as GET /animals?zoo_id=3DZID.</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"8e1140749308">
<li local-id=3D"91084cb41b24">
<p local-id=3D"fa41a4789e36">Status Codes</p></li>
</ol>
<ul local-id=3D"3151f0622450">
<li local-id=3D"5bf2f363c7f8">
<p>200 OK =E2=80=93 [GET]</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"91bac7e16e35">
<p>201 CREATED =E2=80=93 [POST/PUT/PATCH]</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3f8c4fc3717b">
<p>204 NO CONTENT =E2=80=93 [DELETE]</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"298d87203d18">
<p>400 INVALID REQUEST =E2=80=93 [POST/PUT/PATCH]</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fc58185dc482">
<p>404 NOT FOUND =E2=80=93 [*]</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"500e0bf44dd0">
<p>500 INTERNAL SERVER ERROR =E2=80=93 [*]</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e2fc2ffa4c78">Click <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http:=
//www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec10.html" rel=3D"nofollow">http://=
www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec10.html</a> for full information.</=
p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"39591266a339">
<li local-id=3D"7dda244c50a5">
<p local-id=3D"eb0467fd74a9">Error handling</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"2caa1c43f9ad">If status code is 4xx, server should give clie=
nt error message. Key is 'error' and value is error information. E.g.<br>
{<br>
=E2=80=A6<br>
error: "Invalid API key",<br>
=E2=80=A6<br>
}</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7f23e29c2cc1">
<li local-id=3D"2028fbeae324">
<p local-id=3D"e6ce925e814d">Expected Return Documents</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"7e2be6fbb70a">When performing actions using the different HT=
TP verbs to Server endpoints, a Consumer needs to get some sort of informat=
ion in return. This list is pretty typical of RESTful APIs:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"71e71d87ac74">
<li local-id=3D"cffa0df29f07">
<p local-id=3D"a892597ec784">GET /collection: Return a listing (array) of R=
esource objects</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b889ce85277b">
<p local-id=3D"b8fdcda31870">GET /collection/resource: Return an individual=
 Resource object</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a8acb0916a8c">
<p local-id=3D"0e76dfdcf378">POST /collection: Return the newly created Res=
ource object</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"98c880063c75">
<p local-id=3D"a07f6d4683c2">PUT /collection/resource: Return the complete =
Resource object</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d921c4ebc64d">
<p local-id=3D"41c95d88f293">PATCH /collection/resource: Return the complet=
e Resource object</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4c9bb4661895">
<p local-id=3D"ed37076352bb">DELETE /collection/resource: Return an empty d=
ocument</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"4b4af859dcce"><br></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"efbb972cea9b">
<li local-id=3D"dbcf0f9b86bc">
<p local-id=3D"41afc2732321">Hypermedia APIs (optional)</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"d7fbfb9f9038">Giving links in results to make user quickly u=
nderstand what to do next. E.g.<br>
{<br>
...<br>
"link": {<br>
"rel": "collection <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://www.example.c=
om/zoos" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.example.com/zoos</a><span class=3D"co=
nfluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=
=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-external-resource" height=3D"7" wi=
dth=3D"7" src=3D"73a2e9183154d4b949d2be7a1672754c93c0a544b3904881103da52794=
9b62a5" data-image-src=3D"https://engineering.eng.sonicwall.com/images/icon=
s/linkext7.gif" loading=3D"lazy"></span>",<br>
"href": "https://api.example.com/zoos",<br>
"title": "List of zoos",<br>
"type": "application/vnd.yourformat+json"<br>
}<br>
...<br>
} <br>
APIs of Github is this kinds of design, click <a class=3D"external-link" hr=
ef=3D"https://api.github.com/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://api.github.com/</a>=
