uence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156387"></span></span>Support RESTful API wi=
th Django Rest Framework</h3>
<p local-id=3D"9bff973d69de">Django REST framework(DRF) is a powerful and f=
lexible toolkit for building Web APIs. With DRF we can obtain following ach=
ievements easily: <br>
=E2=80=A2 &nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://restframework.he=
rokuapp.com/" rel=3D"nofollow">Web browsable API</a><br>
=E2=80=A2 &nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://www.django-rest-=
framework.org/api-guide/serializers/" rel=3D"nofollow">Serialization</a>&nb=
sp;that supports both&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://www.d=
jango-rest-framework.org/api-guide/serializers#modelserializer" rel=3D"nofo=
llow">ORM</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://www.=
django-rest-framework.org/api-guide/serializers#serializers" rel=3D"nofollo=
w">non-ORM</a>&nbsp;data sources.<br>
=E2=80=A2 &nbsp;Quickly build API views by using or composing a number of p=
re-built views <br>
We're going to create a simple API to allow users to view and add data from=
 aptest_session_group table.</p>
