<h4 local-id=3D"3873655467b6" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-OLE_LINK8OLE_=
LINK9IntegratingDjangowithexistingdatabase"><span class=3D"confluence-ancho=
r-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-OLE_LINK8"><span class=3D"confluenc=
e-anchor-link" id=3D"OLE_LINK8"></span></span><span class=3D"confluence-anc=
hor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-OLE_LINK9"><span class=3D"conflue=
nce-anchor-link" id=3D"OLE_LINK9"></span></span>Integrating Django with exi=
sting database</h4>
<p local-id=3D"1467c01d64c6">Django comes with a utility called inspectdb t=
hat can create models by introspecting an existing database (you have to se=
t this database as 'default' in settings.py). You can view the output by ru=
nning following commands:</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto]# python3 manage.py inspectdb &gt; ap=
i_v1/models.py</p>
<p local-id=3D"cf06c7193a92"><br></p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto]# python3 manage.py makemigrations</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"cfac9351c73f"><br></p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto]#</p>
<p local-id=3D"eac900d4d065"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"S=
onicautoDevelopmentGuide-OLE_LINK16"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link"=
 id=3D"OLE_LINK16"></span></span><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=
=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-OLE_LINK17"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-=
