<h4 local-id=3D"2ff2d2dc07ce" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-Permission">P=
ermission</h4>
<p local-id=3D"d5675fadef90">Together with&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" =
href=3D"https://www.django-rest-framework.org/api-guide/authentication/" re=
l=3D"nofollow">authentication</a>&nbsp;, permissions determine whether a re=
quest should be granted or denied access. Permissions in REST framework are=
 always defined as a list of permission classes. <br>
Before running the main body of the view, each permission in the list is ch=
ecked. If any permission check fails, an exceptions.NotAuthenticated&nbsp;o=
r exceptions.PermissionDenied exception will be raised.<br>
In our project, we use IsAuthenticated and AllowAny permission policy. Sinc=
e every resource is required to be accessible after authentication, we shou=
ld set IsAuthenticated globally, using DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES like blew=
.<br><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-ma=
nual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" height=3D"100" width=3D=
"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"61c674f401f124cb2b8bed229d2e0b4a5d223e4038e70=
b8cd956a50d9de8d886" data-image-src=3D"https://sonicwall.atlassian.net/wiki=
