confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156390"></span></span>Build a DB server=
</h2>
<p local-id=3D"cb7c6ae837b4">We choose PostgreSQL 9.6 and will update to 10=
 in the future. This guide is enable for Red Hat family Linux (including Ce=
ntOS/Fedora/Scientific/Oracle variants). Our production server is a CentOS7=
 with 4 core, 16G memory and 300G hard disk. Dev server can be less powerfu=
l. After installing a brand new CentOS 7, we can set up a PostgreSQL server=
 as follows:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"6f9496056220">
<li local-id=3D"b7c1451cc519">
<p local-id=3D"b52cd37d22d1">Install the repository RPM:</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"a97967eb6aad"><br><span data-colorid=3D"wjg15draac">yum inst=
all </span><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://download.postgresql.o=
rg/pub/repos/yum/9.6/redhat/rhel-7-x86_64/pgdg-centos96-9.6-3.noarch.rpm" r=
el=3D"nofollow"><span data-colorid=3D"uj22ontmzg">https://download.postgres=
ql.org/pub/repos/yum/9.6/redhat/rhel-7-x86_64/pgdg-centos96-9.6-3.noarch.rp=
m</span></a><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embe=
dded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-extern=
al-resource" height=3D"7" width=3D"7" src=3D"73a2e9183154d4b949d2be7a167275=
4c93c0a544b3904881103da527949b62a5" data-image-src=3D"https://engineering.e=
ng.sonicwall.com/images/icons/linkext7.gif" loading=3D"lazy"></span></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"a477209535a8">
<li local-id=3D"6434d910a8d8">
<p local-id=3D"e8621bdaa20b">Install the client packages:</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"f0fa4f914ce8"><br><span data-colorid=3D"dds0l9yiex">yum inst=
all postgresql96</span></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"e721097fdb7b">
<li local-id=3D"3b665b9d56ca">
<p local-id=3D"79bfe55602cd">Install the server packages:</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"e777c69a40e1"><br><span data-colorid=3D"xqisl6d6rx">yum inst=
all postgresql96-server</span></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"12e1bbedb873">
<li local-id=3D"335e6961fc67">
<p local-id=3D"e3dedb91fadd">Initialize the database and enable automatic s=
tart:</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"d1d8cc591280"><br><span data-colorid=3D"koryt00ubn">/usr/pgs=
ql-9.6/bin/postgresql96-setup initdbsystemctl enable postgresql-9.6systemct=
l start postgresql-9.6</span></p>
