lass=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156391"></span></span>Export/Im=
port Sonicauto DB</h2>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"cfbfbb499f15">
<li local-id=3D"5018fc835b46">
<p local-id=3D"9841ff9e0881">Login autodb(10.203.15.9/24)</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"81a26a01d196">Call Gavin for user/password. Then export all =
database. Use " df -h" to make sure there is enough space.</p>
<p>[root@autodb ~]# df =E2=80=93h</p>
<p local-id=3D"8f718b0ec57c"><br></p>
<p>[root@autodb ~]# cd backup/</p>
<p local-id=3D"174e6892f5ea"><br></p>
<p>[root@autodb ~]# pg_dumpall -c | gzip &gt; autodb.20180918.gz</p>
<p local-id=3D"338748211957"><br></p>
<p local-id=3D"4fcf92419571"><br></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"8e0a32c62998">
<li local-id=3D"e47ce63e72eb">
<p local-id=3D"6ec1c9417306">Improt data to new PostgreSQL Server</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"79ebc8a7832c">Login new-installed PC and then scp <span data=
-colorid=3D"s3j6tte1vn">autodb.20180918.gz</span> from autodb to local disk=
.<br>
Import data to database.</p>
<p>[root@localhost ~]# gunzip -c autodb.20180918.gz | psql -U postgres -d p=
ostgres</p>
<p local-id=3D"6af9f9a434c6"><br></p>
<p local-id=3D"1bda15ef084d"><br></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"f41a7a0906aa">
<li local-id=3D"fbc0672f45ef">
<p local-id=3D"581224b43d40">Verify new DB</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"da83be9509b1"><br></p>
<p>[root@localhost ~]# psql -U sonicauto</p>
