k" id=3D"_Toc56156397"></span></span>Install qbs command</h3>
<p local-id=3D"b748a6cd41f1">Since we use 64bit Centos7 here and QBS is 32b=
it, we have to install 32bit package first.</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend SWIFT4.0]# yum install</p>
<p local-id=3D"472461db0ead"><span data-colorid=3D"s4yvdobpwp">libstdc++.i6=
86</span> <br>
Copy /usr/local/bin/qbs* files from other testbed to /usr/local/bin/, and c=
hange file permission to 777.</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend SWIFT4.0]# chmod 777 /usr/local/bin/qbs*</p>
<p local-id=3D"3080265b248c"><br>
Add 'export QBSHOST=3D10.203.15.14' to /root/.bashrc and 'source /root/.bas=
hrc'. And then, we can use qbs commands on the server. <br>
Then, create private ssh key in /root/.ssh/id_rsa and add it to qbsauto ser=
ver's /root/.ssh/authorized_keys</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend ~]# ssh-keygen -t rsa -C "youremail@example.com=
"</p>
<p local-id=3D"5e1afc26462d"><br></p>
