>
<p local-id=3D"aa734558bd19">The last step of building a Django application=
 is deploying it to a production server.<br>
In our project, we choose '<strong>python3.6.6 + Centos7 + Ngnix +Uwsgi + D=
jango2.1</strong>' mode to deploy sonicauto3.0.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"f526066fc9dd" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc56156408G=
etprojectfromsonicgit"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"Sonicau=
toDevelopmentGuide-_Toc56156408"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=
=3D"_Toc56156408"></span></span>Get project from sonicgit</h2>
<p local-id=3D"b974f6506079"><br>
Before deploy, please do the following work to get the Django project from =
sonicgit. <br>
(1) generate public ssh key of your server (already done in chapter 4.3.2)<=
br>
(2) add this key to your own git account<br>
(3) ask project admin to give you appropriate permission<br>
(4) this project will show up in your own git account<br>
(5) execute following commands</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend ~]# mkdir =E2=80=93p /opt/django/sonicauto/</p>
<p local-id=3D"01c5a8885b93"><br></p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend ~]# cd /opt/django/sonicauto/</p>
<p local-id=3D"73c76ac65dda"><br></p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto]# git clone</p>
<p local-id=3D"1a3ad7e08e5c"><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"mailto:git@=
sonicgit.eng.sonicwall.com:SonicAuto/sonicauto.git" rel=3D"nofollow">git@so=
nicgit.eng.sonicwall.com:SonicAuto/sonicauto.git</a></p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto]# mkdir log</p>
<p local-id=3D"9dac1fe3e0b3"><br><br>
The directory structure of this project demo is given below. What needs ill=
ustration is that the outer&nbsp;sonicauto/&nbsp;root directory is just a c=
ontainer for your project. And the inner&nbsp;sonicauto/&nbsp;directory is =
the actual Python package for your project which means it is project name. =
<br><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-man=
ual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" height=3D"375" width=3D"=
