></span></span>Deploy backend by Docker</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"36dd84efe848" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876686_=
Toc55217157_Toc55551814_Toc56156423Dockeroverview"><span class=3D"confluenc=
e-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876686"><span class=3D=
"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc28876686"></span></span><span class=3D"c=
onfluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc55217157"><span =
class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55217157"></span></span><span cl=
ass=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc55551814=
"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55551814"></span></span>=
<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc=
56156423"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156423"></span=
></span>Docker overview</h2>
<p local-id=3D"e165b6e8ba90">Docker Engine is an open source containerizati=
on technology for building and containerizing your applications. Docker Eng=
ine acts as a client-server application with: <br>
=E2=80=A2 A server with a long-running daemon process dockerd.<br>
=E2=80=A2 APIs which specify interfaces that programs can use to talk to an=
d instruct the Docker daemon.<br>
=E2=80=A2 A command line interface (CLI) client docker. <br>
The CLI uses Docker APIs to control or interact with the Docker daemon thro=
ugh scripting or direct CLI commands. Many other Docker applications use th=
e underlying API and CLI. The daemon creates and manage Docker objects, suc=
h as images, containers, networks, and volumes. <br><br><br></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"b1ba9a965b78" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876687_=
Toc55217158_Toc55551815_Toc56156424Preparation"><span class=3D"confluence-a=
nchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876687"><span class=3D"co=
nfluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc28876687"></span></span><span class=3D"conf=
luence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc55217158"><span cla=
ss=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55217158"></span></span><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc55551815"><=
span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55551815"></span></span><sp=
an class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc561=
56424"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156424"></span></=
span>Preparation</h2>
<p local-id=3D"126b43c8b0b5">Before dockerize backend or deploy backend by =
docker, host server must have following configurations according to chapter=
 4. <br>
=E2=80=A2 configure mount point on host machine.<br>
=E2=80=A2 create private ssh key in /root/.ssh/id_rsa and add it to qbsauto=
 server's /root/.ssh/authorized_keys.<br>
=E2=80=A2 install docker and docker-compose on host machine</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"874d90a8ce9c" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876688_=
Toc55217159_Toc55551816_Toc56156425Dockerizebackend"><span class=3D"conflue=
nce-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876688"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc28876688"></span></span><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc55217159"><=
span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55217159"></span></span><sp=
an class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc555=
51816"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55551816"></span></=
span><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide=
-_Toc56156425"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc56156425"><=
/span></span>Dockerize backend</h2>
<p local-id=3D"447cf3c3f5ca">Our project code is located in /opt/django/son=
icauto.</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend ~]# mkdir /opt/django/sonicauto_back_docker</p>
<p local-id=3D"8d4e405a7214"><br></p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend ~]# cd /opt/django/sonicauto_back_docker</p>
<p local-id=3D"73f51426ca01"><br></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"82063ab381c5" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876689_=
Toc55217160_Toc55551817_Toc56156426PullbaseimagefromDockerHub"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876689"><=
span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc28876689"></span></span><sp=
an class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc552=
17160"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55217160"></span></=
span><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide=
-_Toc55551817"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc55551817"><=
/span></span><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopm=
entGuide-_Toc56156426"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_Toc561=
56426"></span></span>Pull base image from DockerHub</h3>
<p local-id=3D"07fa857d4ed9">Pull and run docker image 'centos/python-36-ce=
ntos7' from DockerHub, do some testbed-related configuration in the contain=
er. <br>
=E2=80=A2 configure P4<br>
=E2=80=A2 install QBS command<br>
=E2=80=A2 edit /root/.bashrc</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto_back_docker]# docker container run -i=
t centos/python-36-centos7 bash</p>
<p local-id=3D"c995e6d11548"><br><span data-colorid=3D"ccqsn8ie06">(app-roo=
t)</span><br><span data-colorid=3D"pwr5ui3gzt"># do configuration inside co=
ntainer</span><br><span data-colorid=3D"ztv7yhp4gg">(app-root)exit</span> <=
br>
Then save this container to a new image 'centos7-py36-base:0.0.1'. This ima=
ge can be reused directly when others want to setup a local testbed.</p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto_back_docker]# docker commit ContainID=
 centos7-py36-base:0.0.1</p>
<p local-id=3D"898a4b27ec54"><br></p>
<p>[root@sonicauto3-backend sonicauto_back_docker]#</p>
<p local-id=3D"f80441aa3c70"><span data-colorid=3D"jitd08l040">docker save =
centos7-py36-base:0.0.1 &gt; ./centos7-py36-base.tar</span></p>
<p local-id=3D"1674a1aca812"><br></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"477f165cbb69" id=3D"SonicautoDevelopmentGuide-_Toc28876690_=
